                        


Item #:  SCP-5315

Object Class:  Euclid

Special Containment Procedures: 

Due to its immobile nature, Area-5315 was constructed around SCP-5315 and is to be manned by forces and D-Class personnel. No personnel are to enter SCP-5315 through any doors or windows, and opening the main door from any point is strictly prohibited unless for research purposes.

Native flora has been planted around SCP-5315 and Area-5315 to obstruct it from view from any nearby roads. Electric barbed wire fences enclose an area of 1.5 square kilometers around SCP-5315.

Should any entity exit SCP-5315 from any point, it is to be tracked, neutralized, and cremated immediately. If any studies are done on an emerging entity, hazmat suits are to be worn and termination of the entity followed by cremation is to be carried out as soon as possible.

Should any personnel decide to enter SCP-5315 through the main entrance, they are to equip proper protection and hazmat suits and proceed with decontamination protocols when entering or exiting SCP-5315.

Description:  SCP-5315 is a horse barn found in ████, Michigan. Its dimensions equate to roughly 30’x40’x30’. It is constructed almost entirely from oak and has been painted red with white highlights on supports or moldings, though the paint has chipped and faded due to age. SCP-5315 contains a large, main door, a back door, and a window situated above the main door which could be used to access the loft.

If one attempts to enter or exit SCP-5315 through the back door or window, they will find themselves in a, by all accounts, normal barn ideal for up to two horses. However, should an individual attempt to enter or leave through the main entrance, they will instead open a gateway to a random time and location in Earth’s history. In the location SCP-5315 leads to, there is a frame of a barn door leading to the current time and location. If barn door closes, the rift to the time and locations closes. It’s unknown what happens to the doorframe before or after the barn door closes, as there is no way to exchange data prior to or following the opening or closing of SCP-5315. During no research thus far has SCP-5315 opened to an area inhospitable for terrestrial life.

The main door to SCP-5315 will automatically open once every thirty five days for a duration of eighteen minutes before automatically. It is unknown how or why it does this. If the main door of SCO-5315 is opened manually it will remain open unless manually closed. Attempts to close SCP-5315 manually when it opens automatically show the doors will not move.
